# Quality checks – Automatic when generating code

**NEVER** on the host after code changes: `make format`, `make lint-fix`, `make lint-type`, `make lint-complete`, `make test`, or bare `poetry run pytest`. **ONLY** `make agent-checks`, `make agent-lint`, or `make agent-test` (with `t=` when scoped).

Whenever you **generate or change code** (new feature, refactor, fix), **automatically** run:

```bash
make agent-checks t='tests/...'
```

Use a **narrow `t=` path** for tests related to what you changed (same idea as `make test t='...'`). Omit `t` only when a full suite run is intentional.

## What `make agent-checks` does

Single entry point for agents:

1. **`agent-ensure-env`** — if `api` or `database` is not running, runs `docker compose up -d api database` (silent).
2. **`agent-lint`** — inside **`api`**: `ruff check --fix`, `mypy src`, `ruff format` (same core as `lint-complete`, **without** pre-commit; pre-commit needs git on the host).
3. **`agent-test`** — pytest + coverage (see **docker-compose.mdc** for where it runs and DB connectivity).

Do **not** run `make format`, `make lint-fix`, `make lint-type`, `make lint-complete`, or ad-hoc `poetry run pytest` on the host after changing code. Use **`make agent-checks`** only.

If any step fails, fix the code and re-run until it passes.

## Boundaries (see agent-boundaries.mdc)

- Do not run `make migrate`, `make rollback`, or deployment commands (`make build`, `make stop`, etc.) unless the user asks.
- `make create-migration` only with **user approval**; never `git add` / `commit` / `push`.
- **`make agent-checks`** (and **`agent-ensure-env`**) may start containers when they are down; agents must not call `make start` / `make build` directly for checks—only `make agent-checks`.

## Goal

After every code change, agents run **`make agent-checks`** with a focused `t=` when possible, and fix failures until green.
